  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe mid/upper-level pattern remains relatively unchanged from \nyesterday, with the apex of the subtropical ridge now shifting into \nthe Upper Midwest. The Omega Block situated across the Lower 48 is \nstill intact, but it will begin to collapse over the weekend as an \namplified, neutrally-tilting trough digs eastward into the Desert \nSouthwest. As this occurs, the core of the subtropical ridge will \ncontinue to gradually shift eastward and over the Deep South. This \nwill keep the CWA dry, with warmer high temperatures to follow as \ngeopotential height tendencies rise. Persistence forecasting has \nbeen applied to Saturday and beyond, with the crystal clear sky at \nnight allowing for excellent radiational cooling and the development \nof typical river valley fog. Patchy frost can be expected across the \nhigher terrain each morning through Monday, and the stagnant airmass \nwill maintain calm-to-gentle winds.",
